    "body": "\"Registered with the system\" sounds like \"paired\" to me, but the problem we need to solve in [crbug/1488031](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1488031) is a device that is registered with the system (paired) but has had all of its open connections intentionally closed in order to logically disconnect it.\r\n\r\nI would phrase this here as:\r\n\r\n> [...] it is a wireless serial port and the system has active connections to the wireless device (e.g. an open Bluetooth L2CAP channel).\r\n\r\nIn the `requestPort()` and `getPort()` steps we want to return devices even if `connected` is `false` as calling `port.open()` would establish that connection and in some circumstances that is desirable behavior. For example if the user actively clicked a \"Connect\" button.",
